/_site/
/.quarto/
.DS_Store

**/*.quarto_ipynb
/test-results/

# The panda trainer — corpora, parity fixtures, the Python training env and the
# weights it exports — moved to Ameya-bit/panda-engine on 2026-08-02, and its
# ignore rules moved with it (they described a /trainer/ tree that no longer
# exists here; the last of them claimed the exported weights were committed at
# assets/pandas/engine/policy/, which this repo deliberately does not ship —
# see assets/pandas/engine/README.md). What stays is the one rule about a
# directory that IS here:
#
# npm-linked playwright for the browser gates — a runtime ask, never a
# dependency. It matters because _quarto.yml lists assets/pandas/ as a site
# resource, so anything left under it is swept into _site by a local render.
/assets/pandas/engine/node_modules/

# Figure pipeline scratch. `_data.npz` (6kb) IS committed on purpose — it is what
# lets plot.py restyle every figure without a CPU rerun of the model.
posts/**/figures/__pycache__/
posts/**/figures/compute.log

# The post-render steps. Quarto runs them as scripts, which leaves no bytecode,
# but importing one to test it does — `drop-icons.py`'s tripwire was checked
# that way and left a __pycache__ behind.
tools/**/__pycache__/
/tools/resume/build/
